One harness for every ECDLP method: rho, BSGS, kangaroo, index calculus

Usage: isogeny-tests <COMMAND>

Commands:
  isogeny-evaluate      Complete public-input isogeny evaluation in Rust with FLINT primitives
  scalar-timing         Descriptive local timings of the existing counted scalar multiplication
  endpoint-pairs        Join distinct endpoint workloads without admitting costs or timings
  retained-chain-study  Run the frozen retained-chain probe or complete toy relation pipeline. Counters are raw observations; this command does not admit timings
  diagnostic-preflight  Check pinned diagnostic metadata without launching work
  store                 Push, pull and index large files (factor bases, tables) in the object store
  gpu-stage             Run the existing CUDA ECC binary as a separately labelled GPU stage
  gpu-match             Run CUDA BSGS on a frozen EC Bench workload and verify its scalar here
  gpu-match-verify      Recheck a GPU receipt, raw streams, workload and scalar without a GPU
  calibrate             Check A/A interval coverage and false admissions across quiet and contended sessions
  work                  Price every record of the given session directories in bitop/v1 (docs/units/BITOPS.md): one JSON line per record on stdout
  bitop-vectors         Print the bitop/v1 test vectors (docs/units/bitop-v1.vectors.json), or with `--unit bitop/v2` the bitop/v2 entry widths (docs/units/bitop-v2.vectors.json)
  amortize              Amortise an arm against a rho arm on the same curves, in bitop/v1: per curve, the mean reusable and per-target gates of each, their cost for T targets (rho as one walk that keeps its table, Kuhn and Struik), and the window of target counts in which the arm costs no more (batch rho grows like sqrt(T), so a win is a window, not a threshold)
  methods               List every method with its parameters
  optimize              Inventory and audit the registry-wide optimization loop
  price-units           Measure the full-pricing units (src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/full_prices.json) on this host for Koblitz curves `a:n`, median of `reps` passes each
  wordram-prices        Print the fixed word-RAM reference prices (src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/wordram_price.rs) of the `*_wordram` methods for Koblitz curves `a:n`; nothing is measured
  trend                 Fit how a paired ratio moves across curves (ln ratio against ln r and ln n) from `compare --save` files; JSON to stdout
  sentinels             The frozen replay sentinels (`docs/ecbench/replay-sentinels.json`): one cheap committed record per method id that a pull request replays with `verify --replay-seq`
  host                  Print the host capsule
  plan                  Validate a spec and print what it expands to
  run                   Run a session
  profile-input         Export one exact measured-child input from a frozen spec and sequence
  audit-ir              Replay planned executions of a spec under Callgrind and set each solve's instructions beside its bitop/v1 work (docs/units/BITOPS.md, "What the unit leaves out"): one JSON line per sequence number
  callgrind-ir          Sum the Callgrind Ir parts inside the solve markers
  callgrind-online-ir   Split one profiled solve into reusable, one-target online and tail Ir
  verify                Audit a session from its own files.  Exits 1 when the audit finds a problem (and 2 when it cannot be run at all), so a failed audit fails whatever calls it; a receipt is printed either way
  compare               Compare arm B against arm A
  table                 The one-unit table: every arm on every curve, mean S, ratio to the floor and to the reference arm
  band                  The pricing band of AGENTS.md §5a: every arm's unpriced native work, and any calibration-priced native work, charged alike at each weight (GAE per native operation); pairs ranked only where the order holds at every weight
  wcal                  Measure w_cal (AGENTS.md §5a) by best-of-N timing of a mulmod and a group addition on y^2 = x^3 + a x + b over F_p; prints JSON labelled `best-of-N timing`, never perf-ipc
  resources             Resource vectors for all measured attempts; no invented SAT/GAE conversion
  fb                    Build a factor base and write it with its points
  fbm                   Seal an FBM1 measurement identity (curve × FB1 × oracle × solver × instrument)
  claim                 `vs_rho` claims: one IC run against the strong rho run on one public target, in the report `docs/ic/boundary_targets.json` defines
  db                    The database
  isolab-job            An isolab.job/v1 that runs a spec on an independent lab worker
  bound                 Bound records: what a method costs on a domain, fitted across sizes, sealed and re-derivable (`docs/bounds/README.md`)
  frontier              The frontier of every domain's bounds, and its page
  challenge             Challenges: the frozen paired spec a candidate runs against an incumbent, and the verdict that moves (or does not move) the frontier
  help                  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
